cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite the article (preferred citation)
  and this archive. The code is released under the MIT License; the data,
  tables and figures under CC BY 4.0 (see README.md and LICENSE).
type: software
title: >-
  Code and data for: Background Conditions and Patch Dispersion Shape the Responses to Iron Fertilization in the Subarctic Eastern North Pacific
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
# Placeholder: replace with the DOI that Zenodo assigns at release.
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
# Code: MIT; data, tables and figures: CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE).
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  MATLAB code and processed output of nested ROMS-BEC simulations (1, 4 and
  12 km) of ocean iron fertilization near Ocean Station Papa that reproduce
  Figures 1-4, Supporting Information Figures S1-S13 and Table S1 of the
  article. The plot scripts read only the processed data in data/; the prep
  scripts document how data/ was built from intermediate model products.
keywords:
  - ocean iron fertilization
  - submesoscale
  - marine carbon dioxide removal
  - ROMS
  - BEC
  - biogeochemical modeling
  - Ocean Station Papa
  - subarctic North Pacific
  - MATLAB
